    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have a dataset with measurements on the same individual in different conditions.</div><div><br></div>I know that methylKit does not currently support multiple conditions etc, but is there anything preventing me from manually adding the information on sample pairing to the glm.set.mc.v1 function?<div>That is, changing line 328 in <a href=\"https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/diffMeth.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/diffMeth.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233967544000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jMEHVbC2bCpL_xq1t6_h-\">https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/diffMeth.R</a></div><div>from </div><table style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif,&#39;Segoe UI Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Symbol&#39;;line-height:18.2000007629395px\"><tbody style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre;overflow:visible\">    <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(223,80,0)\">Tmod</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">=</span>model.matrix(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">~</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Treat2</span>)</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;width:50px;min-width:50px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.298039);vertical-align:top;text-align:right;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(238,238,238);border-right-width:1px\"></td></tr></tbody></table>to<div><table style=\"box-sizing:border-box;border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif,&#39;Segoe UI Emoji&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI Symbol&#39;;line-height:18.2000007629395px\"><tbody style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre;overflow:visible\">    <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(223,80,0)\">Tmod</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">=</span>model.matrix(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">~</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">Treat2 + Individual</span>)</td></tr><tr style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><td style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-right:10px;padding-left:10px;width:50px;min-width:50px;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.298039);vertical-align:top;text-align:right;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(238,238,238);border-right-width:1px\"></td></tr></tbody></table><br></div><div>Will this mess up the underlying assumptions of e.g. the SLIM method? Or is there some technical limitation preventing me from doing so?</div><div><br></div><div>The recommendation here: <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/methylkit_discussion/uTcoJ-4Ont0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/methylkit_discussion/uTcoJ-4Ont0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793233967544000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1VzjvnscFC--FGPyVEB3GE\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/methylkit_discussion/uTcoJ-4Ont0</a></div><div>is tricky since I have multiple replicates and would like to use CpG that are not covered in every replicate. I also have a hard time finding an eigenvector corresponding to the individual effect.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div>Lars</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
